Why this license
----------------

The database is built from distances and positions that come from two missions of the
European Space Agency, Gaia and Hipparcos. ESA distributes that data under CC BY-NC 3.0 IGO.
A file that combines several sources follows its most restrictive one, so the whole
database is CC BY-NC 3.0 IGO. Sources with more permissive terms (listed below) are
credited separately and are not affected.

What non-commercial means here
------------------------------

The license says You may not exercise the licensed rights "in any manner that is primarily
intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or private monetary compensation".
Earthlight is a free, ad-free, educational project. It has no revenue and no paid features,
and it must stay that way. If you use the database, you must follow the same terms.

