Papers cited for redshifts
    A redshift for a few record-holding objects (for example GN-z11 and JADES-GS-z14-0) comes
    from published papers, cited by arXiv link in pipeline/curated/deep_sky.yaml. Only a number
    is taken from each. The cosmology and the CMB redshift are from Planck Collaboration 2018 VI.

NASA and JPL
    Planet positions use the approximate orbital elements published by NASA JPL Solar System
    Dynamics (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/approx_pos.html), and reference values come
    from the JPL Horizons system. Credit: NASA/JPL. This is not an endorsement by NASA.

Our own curated data
    The curated deep-sky and history entries (pipeline/curated/) are our own work, with
    summaries written in our own words and a source cited for each entry. They are available
    under the MIT License in their original form in this repository; the database as a whole
    is CC BY-NC 3.0 IGO.

Exact quotes, DOIs, and how each source was checked are recorded in docs/data-sources.md.
